@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bmcar-nouns`
IMPORT `bmcar-insuring-and-period`
IMPORT `bmcar-general-exclusions`
IMPORT `bmcar-general-conditions`
IMPORT `bmcar-section-1`
IMPORT `bmcar-section-2`
IMPORT `bmcar-fixtures`

-- Tests for the construction all risks wording. Every expected value was worked out by
-- hand from the TEXT of the clause cited beside it, before the assertion was run; the
-- arithmetic is written in the comment. None was copied from an evaluation. A failing
-- assertion here is a finding about the source or the encoding, never a value to edit.
--
-- The document prints only three numbers: 14 days (General Condition 5), one month
-- (General Condition 7) and three months (General Condition 8). Each is tested on both
-- sides. Every money figure is a HYPOTHETICAL Schedule figure from bmcar-fixtures.l4:
-- item 1 (works) insured 10 billion, item 2 (plant) 2 billion; Section I deductible 50
-- million, debris sum 200 million, total sum insured 13.5 billion; Section II limit 5
-- billion, deductible 20 million. The occurrence is on 10 June 2026 unless stated.

§ `Tests`

§§ `The insuring agreement and the period of insurance`

-- Insuring agreement (lines 11-14): payment of the premium is a condition.
#ASSERT `the insuring agreement — the premium stated in the Schedule has been paid` `the policy`
#ASSERT NOT `the insuring agreement — the premium stated in the Schedule has been paid` `the policy with the premium unpaid`

-- Lines 44-45: the earlier of works commencing (10 March 2026) and unloading (5 March).
#ASSERT `the date Bao Minh's liability commences` `the policy` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 5)
#ASSERT `the date Bao Minh's liability commences` `the policy before any work or unloading` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "whatever date the Schedule states": works begun 15 February, before the Schedule's 1 March.
#ASSERT `the date Bao Minh's liability commences` `the policy where work began before the Schedule date` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 2 15)
#ASSERT     `the occurrence on` (YMD 2026 2 20) `falls within the period of insurance of` `the policy where work began before the Schedule date`

-- Both sides of the commencement and of the end date (lines 44-45, 51).
#ASSERT NOT `the occurrence on` (YMD 2026 3 4) `falls within the period of insurance of` `the policy`
#ASSERT     `the occurrence on` (YMD 2026 3 5) `falls within the period of insurance of` `the policy`
#ASSERT     `the occurrence on` (YMD 2027 2 28) `falls within the period of insurance of` `the policy`
#ASSERT NOT `the occurrence on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `falls within the period of insurance of` `the policy`
#ASSERT NOT `the occurrence on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `falls within the period of insurance of` `the policy before any work or unloading`
#ASSERT `the date the insurance ends at the latest` `the policy` EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28

-- Line 51-52: an extension agreed in writing.
#ASSERT `the date the insurance ends at the latest` `the policy extended in writing to 31 May 2027` EQUALS YMD 2027 5 31
#ASSERT     `the occurrence on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `falls within the period of insurance of` `the policy extended in writing to 31 May 2027`
#ASSERT     `the occurrence on` (YMD 2027 5 31) `falls within the period of insurance of` `the policy extended in writing to 31 May 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `the occurrence on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `falls within the period of insurance of` `the policy extended in writing to 31 May 2027`

-- Lines 47-48: handed over AND put into use.
#ASSERT     `cover had ended for the damaged part, which had been handed over and put into use` `a loss to a part handed over and put into use`
#ASSERT NOT `cover had ended for the damaged part, which had been handed over and put into use` `a loss to a part handed over but not yet in use`
#ASSERT NOT `cover had ended for the damaged part, which had been handed over and put into use` `a loss to a part in use but not handed over`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to a part handed over and put into use`
#ASSERT     `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to a part handed over but not yet in use`

§§ `General Exclusions`

-- (a): each group is listed; a storm is not.
#ASSERT     `General Exclusion (a) applies to a loss caused by` (LIST `civil war, rebellion, revolution, insurrection or mutiny`)
#ASSERT     `General Exclusion (a) applies to a loss caused by` (LIST `military or usurped power`)
#ASSERT     `General Exclusion (a) applies to a loss caused by` (LIST `the acts of hostile persons acting for or in connection with a political organisation`)
#ASSERT NOT `General Exclusion (a) applies to a loss caused by` (LIST (`a cause the policy does not name, namely` "storm"))
#ASSERT NOT `General Exclusion (a) applies to a loss caused by` (LIST `theft`)

-- Each General Exclusion takes the loss out of Section I cover; the storm loss is the near miss.
#ASSERT     `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `the standard loss to the works`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss caused by war`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss caused by a strike and a storm`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss caused by confiscation`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss caused by radioactive contamination`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss caused by the Insured's wilful negligence`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss caused during a cessation of work`
#ASSERT     `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss by theft`

-- Lines 36-39: the burden shifts to the Insured where the Insured contends exclusion (a)
-- applies; the policy is silent where Bao Minh contends it.
#ASSERT `the party who must prove that the loss or liability is covered, where General Exclusion (a) is contended by` `the Insured` EQUALS `the Insured`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the party who must prove that the loss or liability is covered, where General Exclusion (a) is contended by` `Bao Minh`
        BECAUSE "the policy does not say who must prove cover where Bao Minh contends that General Exclusion (a) applies"

§§ `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent`

#ASSERT     `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `proper conduct of the risk` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `conduct of the risk after an untrue answer` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `conduct of the risk without reasonable precautions` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `conduct of the risk withholding information` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` FALSE
#ASSERT     `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `conduct of the risk with a change notified by telegram and in writing` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `conduct of the risk with a change notified in writing only` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `conduct of the risk with an unapproved change increasing the risk` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `conduct of the risk refusing help with subrogation` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` FALSE
-- General Condition 5(a): telephone OR telegram, AND in writing, AND immediately.
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `proper conduct of the risk` `the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, notice in writing only` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `proper conduct of the risk` `the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, notice on day 2 not immediate` FALSE
-- General Condition 5(b) and the repair-before-inspection rule.
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `proper conduct of the risk` `the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, loss not minimised` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `proper conduct of the risk` `the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, with an early repair` FALSE
-- General Condition 5(e): the police, only for theft.
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `proper conduct of the risk` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` TRUE
#ASSERT     `General Condition 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `proper conduct of the risk` `the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, police informed` TRUE

-- Who bears the cost: General Conditions 3 and 4(b) the Insured; 6 Bao Minh.
#ASSERT `General Condition 3 — the party who bears the cost of the precautions` EQUALS `the Insured`
#ASSERT `General Condition 4(b) — the party who bears the cost of the additional precautions` EQUALS `the Insured`
#ASSERT `General Condition 6 — the party who bears the cost of the acts subrogation requires` EQUALS `Bao Minh`
#ASSERT REFUSED `General Condition 4(b) gives no criteria for adjusting the cover or the premium after a material change` BECAUSE "General Condition 4(b) gives no criteria for adjusting the cover or the premium after a material change"

§§ `General Condition 5 — 14 days`

-- (source lines 102-104)
#ASSERT `the number of days from the occurrence within which Bao Minh must receive notice` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `the last day on which Bao Minh may receive notice of an occurrence on` (YMD 2026 6 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 24
#ASSERT `the last day on which Bao Minh may receive notice of an occurrence on` (YMD 2026 12 25) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 8
#ASSERT `the last day on which Bao Minh may receive notice of an occurrence on` (YMD 2026 2 20) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 6
