#ASSERT     `General Condition 8 — the time-bar after an award has run` `rejected, award of 30 September 2026, no proceedings, as at 31 December 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 8 — the time-bar after an award has run` `rejected, award of 30 September 2026, proceedings on 30 December 2026`
#ASSERT     `General Condition 8 — the time-bar after an award has run` `rejected, award of 30 September 2026, proceedings on 31 December 2026`
#ASSERT     `General Condition 8 — the time-bar after an award has run` `rejected, sole arbitrator's award of 30 September 2026, no proceedings, as at 31 December 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 8 — the time-bar after an award has run` `not rejected, award of 30 September 2026, no proceedings, as at 31 December 2026`

§§ `General Condition 9 — other insurance`

#ASSERT `General Condition 9 — the most Bao Minh pays of` 1_000_000 `at a rateable proportion of` 0.25 EQUALS 250_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `Section I — the outcome of the claim` `the policy` `proper conduct of the risk` (`a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`) `debris` 0 `consequential` 0 `paid before` 0 `other insurance` TRUE `conduct` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` `history` `a clean claim history`)
        BECAUSE "General Condition 9 limits Bao Minh to a rateable proportion that the policy does not define"

§§ `Section I — the insuring clause and the exclusions`

#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to an item not entered in the Schedule`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss that was not sudden and unforeseen`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss that is not physical`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss that needs no repair or replacement`
#ASSERT `Section I — the party who chooses whether to indemnify in cash, by repair or by replacement` EQUALS `Bao Minh`

-- (c) faulty design; (e) corrosion and wear.
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss due to faulty design`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss by corrosion`
-- (f) the plant's own breakdown; near misses: the works damaged by it, and plant damaged by a storm.
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a breakdown of construction plant`
#ASSERT     `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `damage to the works caused by a plant breakdown`
#ASSERT     `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `storm damage to construction plant`
-- (g) vehicles, ships, barges; (h) records, cash and instruments; (i) inventory.
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to a licensed vehicle`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to a barge`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss of cash`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss of drawings`
#ASSERT NOT `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss discovered at an inventory`
-- (d) only the cost of putting right the defective work: 400 million less 100 million.
#ASSERT     `Section I — the loss to the item is covered` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to the works by an accident due to defective workmanship`
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to the works by an accident due to defective workmanship` EQUALS 300_000_000
-- (b) consequential loss is never paid: 1 billion claimed, the occurrence still pays 400 - 50.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the occurrence` `the policy` (`a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`) `debris` 0 `consequential` 1_000_000_000 `paid before` 0 `other insurance` FALSE `conduct` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` `history` `a clean claim history`) EQUALS 350_000_000

§§ `Article 2 — the basis of indemnity`

-- (a) repairable: 400 million necessary, 400 million spent.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `the standard loss to the works` EQUALS 400_000_000
-- (b) total loss: 6 billion less 500 million salvage = 5.5 billion; 7 billion spent replacing.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a total loss of the works so far` EQUALS 5_500_000_000
-- Repair at or above the value is settled as a total loss (lines 240-242).
#ASSERT     `Article 2 — the loss is settled as a total loss` `plant whose repair costs exactly its value`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2 — the loss is settled as a total loss` `plant whose repair costs just under its value`
#ASSERT     `Article 2 — the loss is settled as a total loss` `plant whose repair costs more than its value`
-- 1.2 billion value less 100 million salvage; repair of 1.5 billion is not the basis.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `plant whose repair costs more than its value` EQUALS 1_100_000_000
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `plant whose repair costs exactly its value` EQUALS 1_100_000_000
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `plant whose repair costs just under its value` EQUALS 1_099_999_999
-- Salvage: 400 - 50.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a repair with salvage` EQUALS 350_000_000
-- Only what was actually spent: 300 of 400.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a repair that cost less than the estimate` EQUALS 300_000_000
-- Improvements never paid: 450 spent - 100 improvements = 350.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a repair with improvements` EQUALS 350_000_000
-- Provisional repair that added cost: 430 - 30 = 400.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a repair with a provisional repair that added cost` EQUALS 400_000_000
-- Only what the sum insured includes: 400 - 80.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss partly outside the sum insured` EQUALS 320_000_000
-- Payment waits for the invoices.
#ASSERT     `Article 2 — Bao Minh is not yet bound to pay for the loss to the item` `a repair not yet documented`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2 — Bao Minh is not yet bound to pay for the loss to the item` `the standard loss to the works`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the policy states no time within which Bao Minh must pay a Section I claim` BECAUSE "the policy states no time within which Bao Minh must pay a Section I claim"

§§ `Article 3 — overtime, both ways`

-- Not agreed: 460 spent - 60 overtime = 400. Agreed in writing in advance: 400 + 60 = 460.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a repair with overtime` EQUALS 400_000_000
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy with overtime agreed` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a repair with overtime` EQUALS 460_000_000

§§ `Article I — the sum insured and the average`

-- Item 1: contract 12 billion + principal 0.5 billion = 12.5 billion required; 10 billion
-- insured; 400 x 10 / 12.5 = 320 million.
#ASSERT `Article I — the sum for which the item should have been insured` `a loss to underinsured works` EQUALS 12_500_000_000
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to underinsured works` EQUALS 320_000_000
-- The principal's materials count: 10 + 2.5 = 12.5 billion; the same 320 million.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to works whose principal-supplied materials were left out` EQUALS 320_000_000
-- Sum insured equal to the required sum: no average.
#ASSERT `Article I — the sum for which the item should have been insured` `the standard loss to the works` EQUALS 10_000_000_000
-- Item 2: 2 billion against 2.5 billion new; 400 x 0.8 = 320 million.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to underinsured plant` EQUALS 320_000_000
-- The measure missing, or an item the clause does not cover: declined by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to works whose value at completion is not established`
        BECAUSE "the full contract value of the works at completion has not been established"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to plant whose replacement value is not established`
        BECAUSE "the replacement value of the item by a new item of the same kind and capacity has not been established"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss to item 4`
        BECAUSE "Article I states the sum insured required for items 1, 2 and 3 only"
-- An excluded loss never reaches Article I, so a missing measure does not matter there.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a loss due to faulty design` EQUALS 0

-- The item's sum insured caps: 1.9 billion repair + 300 million agreed overtime = 2.2
-- billion, against a sum insured of 2 billion. Without the agreement, 1.9 billion.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy with overtime agreed` (YMD 2026 6 10) `plant repaired at 2.2 billion with overtime` EQUALS 2_000_000_000
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `plant repaired at 2.2 billion with overtime` EQUALS 1_900_000_000

§§ `Section I — the occurrence: deductible, debris, limits`

-- 400 - 50 deductible.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the occurrence` `the policy` (`a standard claim for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`)) EQUALS 350_000_000
-- 30 million is below the 50 million deductible.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the occurrence` `the policy` (`a standard claim for` (LIST `a small loss to the works`)) EQUALS 0
-- A per-occurrence limit of 300 million.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the occurrence` `the policy with a per-occurrence limit of 300 million` (`a standard claim for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`)) EQUALS 300_000_000
-- Debris: 250 million cost against a 200 million separate sum: 350 + 200.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the occurrence` `the policy` (`a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`) `debris` 250_000_000 `consequential` 0 `paid before` 0 `other insurance` FALSE `conduct` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` `history` `a clean claim history`) EQUALS 550_000_000
-- Debris of 150 million: 350 + 150.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the occurrence` `the policy` (`a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`) `debris` 150_000_000 `consequential` 0 `paid before` 0 `other insurance` FALSE `conduct` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` `history` `a clean claim history`) EQUALS 500_000_000
-- No separate sum in the Schedule: no debris cover.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the occurrence` `the policy with no sum for debris` (`a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`) `debris` 150_000_000 `consequential` 0 `paid before` 0 `other insurance` FALSE `conduct` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` `history` `a clean claim history`) EQUALS 350_000_000
-- No covered loss: no debris either.
#ASSERT `Section I — the reimbursement of the cost of clearing debris` `the policy` (`a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` (LIST `a loss due to faulty design`) `debris` 150_000_000 `consequential` 0 `paid before` 0 `other insurance` FALSE `conduct` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` `history` `a clean claim history`) EQUALS 0
-- Aggregate: 13.3 billion paid before leaves 200 million of the 13.5 billion.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the occurrence` `the policy` (`a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`) `debris` 0 `consequential` 0 `paid before` 13_300_000_000 `other insurance` FALSE `conduct` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` `history` `a clean claim history`) EQUALS 200_000_000
-- Two items: works 400 + plant 320 (averaged) = 720; less 50 = 670; plus debris 150 = 820.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the occurrence` `the policy` (`a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`, `a loss to underinsured plant`) `debris` 150_000_000 `consequential` 0 `paid before` 0 `other insurance` FALSE `conduct` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` `history` `a clean claim history`) EQUALS 820_000_000
-- An excluded item adds nothing: works 400 + plant breakdown 0, less 50.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the occurrence` `the policy` (`a standard claim for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`, `a breakdown of construction plant`)) EQUALS 350_000_000

